## Engineering standards

This project follows the cross-project engineering standards from `pulsarules_codex` (rules,
patterns, workflows), rendered as skills under `{{.SkillsDir}}/`. When a rule or pattern is
ambiguous, fall back to the Effective Go / Code Review Comments baseline.

## Mandatory routing contract (read before any Go/SQL/config change)

opencode has no SessionStart hook, so this contract is stated here instead: ANY Go/SQL/config change
MUST begin by consulting the `project-router` skill (`{{.SkillsDir}}/project-router/SKILL.md`):
classify the task against its dispatch table, LOAD every matched skill, and APPLY each skill's rules
WHILE writing (not as an afterthought). Baseline always applies: `go-style`, `errors-logging`,
`code-placement`, `code-minimalism`. Load `integration-tests` for ANY `_test.go`. Tests are
same-package, one `_test.go` per source file, table-driven (`testCases`/`testCase`, never `tt`),
cover every failure path, and use `testing/synctest` for time (never a `now func()` clock field). No
em dash (U+2014) in `.go`. Before committing, run each loaded skill's Validation checklist and the
verify suite (`go build && go vet && go test -race`, golangci-lint, `gofmt -l`).

